decant engine
=============

This directory is the wine 11 + DXMT install/launch recipe used by the
decant macOS app. It lives in the same git tree as the SwiftUI front end.

Upstream base
-------------
Derived from steam-on-m1-wine
Copyright (c) 2026 notpop
Licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
Source: https://github.com/notpop/steam-on-m1-wine
Pinned base revision when imported: 540037e

Local changes on top of that base include:
  - default paths under ~/Library/Application Support/decant
  - writable Wine deploy via cp -RX into engines/wine11
  - bison/flex on PATH for Wine rebuilds
  - skipping the separate "Steam on M1 Wine.app" dock installer
    (decant.app is the product UI)
  - deploy of this recipe into Application Support on install
  - prefix-scoped process cleanup (wineserver -k + WINEPREFIX filter)
  - version pins recorded in engine/PINS.md

See engine/PINS.md for Wine / DXMT / LLVM / recipe SHAs.

================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

This recipe orchestrates third-party software. THIS TREE NEITHER
REDISTRIBUTES NOR BUNDLES THEIR BINARIES OR FULL SOURCE — components
are installed through upstream channels or downloaded at setup time.

Wine (stable)
    License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
    Source:  https://www.winehq.org/
    Notes:   Installed via Homebrew Cask wine-stable, then copied into
             decant's engine home. The optional -fvisibility=default
             rebuild clones Wine source at tag wine-11.0 and replaces
             only winemac.so.

Winetricks
    License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
    Source:  https://github.com/Winetricks/winetricks

DXMT
    License: MIT License
    Copyright: (c) 2023 Feifan He
    Source:  https://github.com/3Shain/dxmt
    Notes:   scripts/04-install-dxmt.sh fetches a release tarball.
             scripts/07-build-dxmt-fork.sh builds notpop/dxmt branch
             debug/present-path-tracing (mutable branch; pin when possible).

GStreamer runtime
    License: LGPL-2.1
    Source:  https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org/

Steam client (installed on demand)
    License: Steam Subscriber Agreement
    Notes:   Fetched from Valve's CDN at runtime.

Build-time tools (Homebrew, mingw-w64, LLVM 15, meson, etc.) are invoked
by the scripts and are not redistributed in this repository.
